    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "This beautifully appointed 125.96 sq.m. detached bungalow offers an exceptional blend of space, privacy, and scenic beauty on an elevated 1-acre site with stunning views of the Shannon Estuary. Built in the 1980s with durable twin-leaf block construction, this five-bedroom home boasts a generous and versatile layout, including an inviting entrance hallway, a cozy sitting room, an expansive open-plan kitchen/dining/living area, a practical utility with a guest toilet, a central corridor, and a modern family shower room. Serviced by a dual oil and solid fuel heating system, a private well, and an on-site septic tank, the property promises efficient, self-sufficient country living. Reached via a private avenue well set back from the public link road, the mature, tree-lined site delivers unmatched seclusion while providing ample space and potential for a detached garage or workshop. Nestled in a highly sought-after countryside location, you will enjoy peaceful rural surroundings just moments from Tarbert village and its excellent amenities, including primary and comprehensive schools. Vacant for approximately nine years, this property presents a rare opportunity for discerning buyers. Making an early viewing highly advised to truly appreciate its full extent and potential.  Strictly by appointment - contact Dillon Prendiville Auctioneers today to arrange a viewing - call 068 21739."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Rooms",
        "SortOrder": 2,
        "Content": "Entrance Hall - 4.0m x 1.5m \r\nTiled floor and recessed built-in cloak with radiator.\r\n\r\nSitting Room - 4.6m x 3.4m \r\nFitted carpet, solid fuel stove with marble fireplace with timber surround and recessed built-in display.  Dual aspect overlooking the gardens and surrounding countryside.\r\n\r\nKitchen/Dining/Living Area - 9.0m x 3.2m \r\nTiled floor, fully fitted kitchen with stainless steel sink with double drainer and tiled splash back.  Living area with solid fuel Stanley range and recessed hot-press.\r\n\r\nRear Entrance Lobby/Utility - 3.0m x 1.5m \r\nTiled floor and plumbed for washing machine.\r\n\r\nToilet - 1.4m x 1.8m \r\nTiled floor with toilet, wash basin and frosted window\r\n\r\nCloak Room - 1.5m x 1.2m \r\nWith attic access hatch.\r\n\r\nCorridor - 9.0m x 1.0m \r\n\r\n\r\nBedroom 1 - 2.9m x 2.4m \r\nWith laminate floor and built-in recessed wardrobes.\r\n\r\nBedroom 2 - 2.9m x 2.5m \r\nWith laminate floor and built-in recessed wardrobes.\r\n\r\nBedroom 3 - 2.9m x 2.4m \r\nWith laminate floor and built-in recessed wardrobes.\r\n\r\nShower Room - 1.7m x 3.2m \r\nWith tiled floor and tiled splash back areas. Complete with toilet, wash basin and vanity unit.\r\n\r\nBedroom 4 - 4.0m x 2.8m \r\nWith laminate floor and built-in floor to ceiling wardrobes.\r\n\r\nBedroom 5 - 4.2m x 3.2m \r\nWith fitted carpet and built-in floor to ceiling wardrobes.\r\n\r\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Double glazed golden oak PVC Windows and doors.\r\nDual heating system of oil and solid fuel.\r\nSpacious and light filled accommodation.\r\nLarge mature site with tree lined boundary.\r\nGreat potential for gardening or DIY enthusiast.\r\nAmple space for garage or shed.\r\nOn-site private water and on-site septic tank.\r\nElevated private site with private avenue from the public road.\r\nPVC fascia and soffit - pumped wall cavity insulation and attic insulation.\r\nConcrete driveway and rear yard.\r\nTarbert 2.8 km, Listowel 20 km, Ballybunion seaside 24 km & Limerick city 54 km"
      },
